{"id": "EUVD-2026-103610", "enisaUuid": "fd228587-f186-310d-a414-8b76f0b36a54", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: dsa: mt7530: fix NULL dereference on unbind of MT7531 and MT7621\n\nThe core and io supplies are only requested for ID_MT7530: both the\ndevm_regulator_get() in probe and the regulator_enable() in\nmt7530_setup() are guarded by the switch id, but mt7530_remove()\ndisables them unconditionally. On an MT7621 or an MT7531 both pointers\nare still NULL from devm_kzalloc(), so rmmod or a sysfs unbind calls\nregulator_disable() on NULL.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd172580e624bac00d83abd5c4320d2e14d853bc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9a5298532780ecdd05c3220f3e1e3067b3537c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62c0e38b2e5034184d4502ce77bd178b29e59b83", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aae2a1f1e3a0ac5eeb439262a2328a2a392413ac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c2cdef41e0b4d8ed23a5b41e6ad4e64594e055e4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4r34-63x3-rq2x", "CVE-2026-98565"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "18abffdf-54d6-3c26-9ab2-87a0cdb2d528", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "1cbf2bef-dcb6-362d-8c3f-6176c35add45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.1"}, {"id": "323fc931-d765-3bf0-b5d2-daa6a0daecb7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddda1ac116c852bb969541ed53cffef7255c4961 <e9a5298532780ecdd05c3220f3e1e3067b3537c3"}, {"id": "41796a09-d17a-3789-a21c-db06bc38f3c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "613c21ce-2860-39a5-b947-65f5f60e117c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddda1ac116c852bb969541ed53cffef72